# Unity Project Rules

## Language & conventions

- **C# only.** PascalCase types/methods, camelCase locals, `_camelCase` private fields.
- **`[SerializeField] private`** over public fields. Add `[Tooltip]`, `[Range]`, `[Header]`.
- **`TryGetComponent<T>(out var c)`** over `GetComponent<T>() != null`.
- **Cache components** in `Awake`. Never `GetComponent`/`Camera.main`/`Find*` in `Update`.
- **Subscribe in `OnEnable`, unsubscribe in `OnDisable`** — survives pooling.
- **`sealed`** on classes not designed for inheritance.
- **`readonly`/`const`** wherever possible.

## Hot paths — zero allocations

- No `new` in `Update`, `FixedUpdate`, physics callbacks, or `OnGUI`.
- No LINQ in per-frame code.
- No string concatenation/interpolation in loops (use `StringBuilder`).
- No `foreach` over `IEnumerable<T>` — iterate `List<T>` by index.
- Cache `WaitForSeconds`, delegates, and buffers.
- Use **`NonAlloc` physics query variants** (`RaycastNonAlloc`, `OverlapSphereNonAlloc`).
- Use **`sqrMagnitude`** over `Distance` for comparisons.
- **Never `Camera.main`** in `Update`.

## Unity API discipline

- **`Resources.Load` is banned** in shipping code. Use **Addressables**.
- **`Instantiate`/`Destroy`** in hot loops → **object pools**.
- **`SendMessage`/`BroadcastMessage`** banned.
- **`Invoke("Method", 1f)`** banned — use UniTask or coroutines.
- **`renderer.material`** in `Update` banned — use `MaterialPropertyBlock` or cache.
- **Never mix old and new Input System** — use **New Input System**.
- **Never set `transform.position`** on a Rigidbody — use `MovePosition`/`velocity`.

## Editor code

- Editor scripts live under **`Editor/`** folders or editor-only asmdefs.
- Guard with **`#if UNITY_EDITOR`** if placed outside.
- Every inspector mutation wrapped in **`Undo.RecordObject`**.
- Progress bars for operations > 1 second.

## Save / network

- **Version every save format** (`version` field, day one).
- **Atomic writes**: temp + replace + `.bak`.
- **Never store `GameObject` refs** in save data — use IDs.
- **Server authority by default.** Client sends intent, never truth.
- **Never trust client input** for authoritative state.

## Perf & platform

- **Profile on target hardware**, not editor.
- **60 FPS = 16.6 ms budget**, target ≤ 50%.
- **URP** by default; HDRP only if explicitly required.
- Precision: `half` on mobile, `float` where needed.
- **Ask target platform** before optimizing.

## Git hygiene

- **Commit `.meta` files always.**
- **Do not commit:** `Library/`, `Temp/`, `Logs/`, `obj/`, `Build/`, `UserSettings/`, `MemoryCaptures/`.
- **Force Text** serialization; **Visible Meta Files**.
- **UnityYAMLMerge** for scene/prefab conflicts.

## Anti-patterns — self-check before finishing

- [ ] No allocations in hot paths
- [ ] No `Find*` / `Camera.main` / `GetComponent` in `Update`
- [ ] No `Instantiate`/`Destroy` in loops
- [ ] No LINQ in per-frame code
- [ ] No `Resources` in shipping
- [ ] Events unsubscribed on disable/destroy
- [ ] Save data versioned + atomic writes
- [ ] Network authority respected
- [ ] Editor code gated (`#if UNITY_EDITOR` or editor asmdef)
- [ ] Platform-appropriate precision/settings
